    "clashSummary": "DRIZZGB & TRAPPY vs F-DON & DAN DANNAH was the **PenGame 2v2 tournament final**, with **£5,000** on the line. The judging panel featured **Professor Green**, **Aitch**, and **Big Narstie**, with the host making clear that this was the main event and the reason everyone had come out.\n\nBefore the battle, the judges explain what they want to see: bars, intelligence, lyrical ability, metaphors, flows, entertainment, and professional battle skills. The stakes are high, and the room treats this like a proper final from the start.\n\nDRIZZGB & TRAPPY open the battle with strong energy, targeting F-DON and DAN DANNAH with direct insults, name flips, gun bars, Birmingham/South angles, and tournament-final pressure. F-DON & DAN DANNAH respond with a more structured and theatrical approach, attacking them as backup dancers, calling out previous battles, and using a gym belt prop to frame one of them as being carried.\n\nAcross the battle, DRIZZGB & TRAPPY show stronger chemistry as a duo. Their second and third rounds are packed with back-to-back switches, shared setups, and fast team transitions. F-DON & DAN DANNAH have strong individual bars, especially around race, appearance, previous battles, and direct threats, but the judges repeatedly point out that the winning side had better synergy.\n\nThe official decision goes to **DRIZZGB & TRAPPY**, who are crowned **PenGame 2v2 Champions**.",
