    "clashSummary": "DEENO vs JM took place during **PenGame Rap Battle 2024**, in front of a major judging panel featuring **Professor Green**, **RD**, and **Big Narstie**. Before the clash starts, the judges make it clear what they want to see: intelligent bars, skill, flows, metaphors, double entendres, rebuttals and proper performance. Big Narstie also warns that he is deducting points for lazy dead-relative material, making it clear that shock value alone will not be enough.\n\nJM wins the coin toss and chooses to go first. From his opening round, he brings high energy, aggression and a direct attempt to dismantle DEENO’s reputation on PenGame. His main angle is that DEENO is not the best at anything on the platform — not the best rapper, not the best ginger, not the best white man, not even the best “fat kid.” It is a blunt but effective way to strip DEENO’s status down early.\n\nDEENO responds with a more grime-heavy performance style. He uses references to **Pop Smoke**, **Ardee**, **Marni**, **Versace**, **Playboi Carti**, and street imagery to bring energy back. However, JM’s pacing, crowd control and pressure keep him ahead for large parts of the clash.\n\nThe battle becomes especially heated in the second and third rounds. JM brings repeated attacks on DEENO’s appearance, weight, teeth, losing streak, Wales/Cardiff identity, and alleged family material. DEENO fires back with freestyle moments, Pride/racism angles, homelessness/Sainsbury’s material, and a “Penge Poseidon” line.\n\nThe judges give the battle to **JM**. RD has JM winning **2-1**, Professor Green also gives it to JM after saying the battle was close until a decisive third-round moment, and Big Narstie effectively points to JM as the winner.",
