    "clashSummary": "JAYCEE vs K.I.M.E took place on the **North vs South PenGame card**, with **Professor Green**, **Aitch** and **Big Narstie** judging. Before the clash, the judges made it clear they wanted proper battle craft: bars, flow, delivery, punchlines, humour, intelligence and clean execution.\n\nJAYCEE wins the coin toss and chooses to go first. He opens with aggression, attacking K.I.M.E’s appearance, teeth, breath, anxiety, lack of status, North background and whether he belongs on the same stage. K.I.M.E responds with a cleaner, more controlled round, attacking JAYCEE as young, fake, privileged, better suited to singing, and not built for battle rap.\n\nThe battle is close. JAYCEE has a lot of writing and some heavy moments, especially in the third. However, K.I.M.E has stronger delivery, better flow control and a more seasoned performance. The judges officially give the battle to **K.I.M.E**, with Aitch calling it **2-1** and Big Narstie also siding with K.I.M.E.",
