        "performer": "DAN DANNAH",
        "overview": "DAN came with a proper competitive performance. His first round had a clean concept: “Who is Orion?” becomes “who is lying?” He attacked ORION’s authenticity, weight, name, hype and tournament status. His second round had more humour, using Goliath/David, circumference, food, edibles and body-image jokes to make ORION look overhyped and physically awkward.\n\nHis third round was his strongest for crowd rhythm. He brought SKAMZ into the performance and turned “DAN” into “dangerous”, creating a chant-style ending. The issue was diction. The judges said there were times where DAN was saying good material, but the clarity made people work too hard to catch it.",
