    "clashSummary": "REN DMC vs SKAMZ was the PenGame Season 4 Final on the Road to Wembley, with £5,000 on the line. SKAMZ won the coin toss and chose to go first, framing the battle as the last stage of his redemption run. REN came in as the showman, the viral name, and the battler who had already turned crowd control into a weapon throughout the tournament.\n\nThis final was closer than the final decision makes it look. SKAMZ had a strong first round and a very effective second round, especially with the “green men” video angle and the attack on REN’s image. But his third round collapse changed everything. He forgot material, restarted, stumbled again, and eventually only delivered a short, damaged round.\n\nREN capitalised perfectly. His first round used the “dad/milk” angle and immediately turned SKAMZ’s own opening into a father-son story. His second round answered the sexuality/green-screen angle with control and rebuttal energy. His third round became a victory lap: legacy talk, PenGame influence, props, reloads, dads, and the final “SKAMZ, get out of here” chant.\n\nThe judges all gave it to REN DMC, making him the PenGame Season 4 Champion.",
