    "clashSummary": "KANDI vs RA'SIAH opened PenGame Cold War Group A, powered by SoundOn. The host introduces the new tournament format, confirms that battles will be dropping every Wednesday and Saturday at 6pm, and shouts out the event sponsors and partners: Chicken Shop, SoundOn, and Platinum Education Services.\n\nThe judging panel is introduced as Lippy Lickshot, Judy, and Joey Clipslaw / Burdys Bars. KANDI is framed as a fan favourite before the battle starts, with one judge saying he has seen KANDI go viral enough times and wants to see that same energy live.\n\nKANDI wins the coin toss and chooses for RA'SIAH to go first. RA'SIAH opens with a character-based first round, painting KANDI as someone acting tougher than he is. He attacks KANDI's image, teeth, relationship rumours, stage persona, race/culture presentation and the idea that KANDI is playing a character.\n\nKANDI responds with a more chaotic and aggressive round, mixing threats, sexual disrespect, family shots, dark shock bars and fast-flow sections. He has energy and crowd reaction, but RA'SIAH stays cleaner, more controlled and more structured across the battle.\n\nThe official judges all give the battle to RA'SIAH.",
