    "clashSummary": "PASSIVE vs RA’SIAH took place in **PenGame Cold War Group A**, powered by **SoundOn**. The host introduces the Cold War tournament and reminds the crowd that the top two from each group will progress to the quarter-finals. This battle lands deep into Group A, with both MCs already having momentum in the tournament.\n\nPASSIVE wins the coin toss and chooses to go first. His opening round is direct, technical and personal, targeting RA’SIAH’s lips, music, beat selection, voice, girlfriend, drug use, style and lack of originality. RA’SIAH responds with a strong first round built around PASSIVE as a producer first and MC second, accusing him of copying grime legends and lacking originality.\n\nThe battle is competitive. PASSIVE’s strongest asset is structure: he has cleaner rounds, clearer setups, and more controlled punch delivery. RA’SIAH’s strength is flow and aggression: he raps with high energy, switches quickly and brings strong rhythm, but some of his later material becomes more sex-angle heavy and less varied.\n\nThe judges give the battle to **PASSIVE**, noting that RA’SIAH likely took the first round but PASSIVE took the later rounds. The host confirms the decision as **2-1 to PASSIVE**.",
