        "overview": "PASSIVE wins by being more consistent across the full battle. His first round is a clean opener with multiple angles: RA’SIAH’s chapped lips, his song about his mum, beat-purchasing history, girlfriend, voice, grind artistry, hairline, race-focused material and alleged repetition. He also uses producer references naturally, which suits his image and lets him attack RA’SIAH’s music taste and delivery.\n\nHis second round is more direct and probably his strongest. He attacks RA’SIAH’s bottom lip, flopping, unclear delivery, drug use, lack of interesting material, Arsenal shirt angle, poverty/money, mum/partner bars, and ends with a sharp run around stealing from RA’SIAH’s mother after giving him a new brother. The round has a solid balance of jokes, disrespect and technical criticism.\n\nHis third round seals the battle. PASSIVE attacks RA’SIAH as a “flipping mess,” says he handles keys at a check-in desk rather than drugs, flips RA’SIAH’s lip into him “tripping on his lip,” criticises his gimmicks and repetition, and lands the **“record, record, record”** section. He then expands into a wider callout lane, saying he has battled too many disabled/youth opponents and calling out other PenGame names, including JAYCEE, GRAMS, STORM, SMIL3Z, PRYNLEE, ORION and REN.\n\nPASSIVE’s biggest strength here is that he sounds like he knows where each round is going. He does not rely on one huge moment; he wins through cleaner construction.",
