      "verdict": "Official Judgement: PASSIVE wins",
      "summary": "There is an official judgement in the transcript.\n\nOne judge says RA’SIAH won the first round, but the last two rounds became too sex-bar heavy and he got tired. That judge gives the battle to PASSIVE. Another judge says round two was weak overall but praises PASSIVE’s rapping and also gives it to PASSIVE. The final summary confirms the result as 2-1 to PASSIVE.\n\nThe judges acknowledge RA’SIAH’s talent, flow and workload, especially given that he had multiple battles on the day, but PASSIVE is judged to have edged the battle through better balance and stronger later rounds.\n\nArchive score: PASSIVE 2-1.\n\nArchive note: RA’SIAH likely took round one with sharper producer/copycat angles, but PASSIVE won the second and third through clearer structure, better direct critique and stronger control. RA’SIAH had high-level flow, but his later rounds leaned too heavily into sex bars and mum angles, allowing PASSIVE to edge the battle."
