    "clashSummary": "KANDI vs SKAMZ took place during **PenGame Cold War Group A**, powered by **SoundOn**. The host introduces the battle as part of a strong opening night for the Cold War tournament, with shout-outs to **SoundOn**, **Chicken Shop**, and **Platinum Education Services**. The wider tournament format is also reinforced, with the top two from each group progressing towards the quarter-finals.\n\nThe battle is built around two chaotic performers, but the difference is clarity. KANDI goes first and brings his usual extreme disrespect, using shock bars, family angles, anime references, sexuality insults, gendered attacks and violent imagery. SKAMZ responds by turning KANDI’s whole style against him, arguing that KANDI says wild things for reaction but often lacks structure, clarity and actual substance.\n\nKANDI has moments. His first round has energy and a clear attempt to mock SKAMZ’s anime lane. His third round has some strong individual flips, including the **AA / battery** line and the ashtray / Drag Race section. But across the battle, his material often becomes scattered and hard to follow.\n\nSKAMZ is more direct. He attacks KANDI’s alleged pimp image, OnlyFans rumours, crowd reaction, reloads, voice-changing, shock-value writing, and his relationship with Bully. The **Bully** section in the third becomes the biggest live-room moment of the battle.\n\nThe judges call it a **whitewash** and give the battle to **SKAMZ 3-0**.",
