        "overview": "KANDI brings the usual chaos, humour and shock value, but the battle is inconsistent. His first round begins with intent, saying he will draw PASSIVE out, but the round is loose and ends with a mic drop. The host has to remind him to concentrate, which immediately hurts the performance.\n\nHis first round still has angles: PASSIVE’s girl, body language, sexuality, his partner looking like his dad, and the idea that PASSIVE is not hard like other battlers. But the writing does not fully settle, and the round feels undercooked compared with PASSIVE’s opener.\n\nKANDI’s second round is much stronger. The **“What in the Butlins holiday is this? What in the emergency housing is this? What in the fridge front garden is this?”** section is one of his best moments. It is funny, class-coded, visual and very KANDI. Even one judge later mentions that line as proper and says it went over people’s heads. KANDI also attacks PASSIVE’s mum, benefits, housing image, and overall background.\n\nHis third round starts with energy and lands some of his strongest material. He goes into “one bar” repetition, Kim Jong Un/career spin, abortion-style shock lines, food/frozen-house imagery, and a strong burst of crowd reaction. However, he overheats and has to stop before fully completing the round. The host confirms he is alright, just overheated, and stresses that the platform cares about the MCs.\n\nKANDI loses, but he does not lose flat. The judges specifically say there is no one who loses like him — he loses with style. His issue is consistency, not impact.",
